# ==============================================================================
# duf CLI Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# This template generates a configuration file for `duf` (Disk Usage Filesystem),
# a modern replacement for `df` with colorful output and JSON support.
#
# The generated content consists of CLI arguments passed to `duf`.
# Each argument must be a valid command-line flag or value accepted by `duf`.
#
# Self-Documentation Guide:
# - args (List[str]): A list of CLI arguments to pass to `duf`.
#   Examples:
#     - --json: Output in JSON format (useful for machine parsing).
#     - --only local: Only show local filesystems (exclude network mounts).
#     - --sort size: Sort output by disk usage.
#   Note: Arguments containing spaces must be quoted as single strings in the list,
#   e.g., '--only local' or 'mount points /dev/sda1'.
# ==============================================================================

# List of CLI arguments to pass to `duf`, one per line (e.g., `--json`, `--only local`, `--sort size`);
# arguments with spaces must be quoted.
{% for arg in (args | default([])) %}{{ arg }}{% if not loop.last %}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}